Pymtheg patch 0009 (C-21, not upstream): macros named like primitive types.

Accepts valid Rust: a macro whose name is a primitive type name
(`str![[r#"..."#]]` from snapbox, `u8!(..)`), in any position a macro
invocation may appear. Macros live in their own namespace, so the name is
not the type. Also a primitive type name with generic arguments as a type
path (`&str<u8, el>`), which is valid syntax (a later name-resolution error
in ordinary code, accepted as proc-macro input).
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/macros.html#macro-invocation
           https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/paths.html#paths-in-types
Upstream issue: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/issues/322
(open; this is the fix the issue proposes). No upstream pull request.

